The '''Akzani''' are {{WF|Mirage}}'s [[Signature Weapons|signature]] rapid firing dual pistols that rely on deep magazines to fuel its high projectile count per second. While they deal low damage per bullet, they sport a larger ammo reserve than other similar pistols which can help relieve ammo inefficiency.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon primarily deals {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Innate {{Pol|Naramon}} polarity.

{{Advantages|}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Lowest base damage of all secondaries.
**Second lowest base damage per bullet of all secondaries, after {{Weapon|Twin Grakatas}}.
*Very inefficient ammo economy.
}}

==Acquisition==
The Akzani's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*Currently, Akzani lacks a [[Signature Weapon]] bonus with {{WF|Mirage}}/{{WF|Mirage Prime}}.
*With a maxed rank {{M|Trick Mag}} mod, the Akzani can increase its capacity to hold 760 rounds of ammo.
*The Akzani have very similar stats to the {{Weapon|Dex Furis}}, though the former has lower overall damage and half status chance.

==Trivia==
*Currently, there is no single "Zani" variant.
*Despite being the favored pistols of {{WF|Mirage}}, {{WF|Mirage Prime}} did not feature an Akzani "Prime", instead she wielded the {{Weapon|Akbolto Prime}} as her weapon of choice.
*This is the first secondary weapon to feature a default extended ammunition size.
*This is the third secondary weapon said to have been favored by a specific Warframe. First was {{Weapon|Akbolto}} with {{WF|Nyx}} and second was {{Weapon|Twin Vipers}} with {{WF|Banshee}} as limited time bundles.
*The word "Zani" is derived from the ''[[wikipedia:Zanni|zanni]]'', a character type in the ''[[wikipedia:Commedia dell'arte|Commedia dell'arte]]'' known as an astute servant or trickster. The [[wikipedia:Harlequin|Harlequin]] (the source for {{WF|Mirage}}'s overall design) is one of the most well-known ''zanni''.
*To reload, the small magazines slide up through the top of the weapon and then slide back in. The player will also angle the weapons forward, which gives the illusion the weapon itself is animated.

