'''Akstiletto Prime''' is the [[Prime]] variant of the {{Weapon|Akstiletto}} dual machine-gun pistols, featuring higher damage, [[critical multiplier]], [[status chance]], magazine, and ammo capacity, at some expense to [[fire rate]] and [[critical chance]]. It was released alongside {{WF|Vauban Prime}} and {{Weapon|Fragor Prime}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Impact}} damage.
*Can use the Akstiletto Prime-exclusive {{M|Zazvat-Kar}} mod.

{{Advantages|}}
{{Disadvantages|}}

{{WeaponComparison|Akstiletto}}
==Acquisition==
{{PrimeTable}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

===Vaultings===
*On [https://forums.warframe.com/topic/932951-last-chance-for-vauban-prime/ March 14, 2018], it was announced that Akstilleto Prime, alongside {{WF|Vauban Prime}} and {{Weapon|Fragor Prime}}, would enter the [[Prime Vault]] and be retired from the reward tables on March 20, 2018. Any preexisting components or fully-built weapons will remain as is.
*Akstilleto Prime resurfaced along with {{WF|Vauban Prime}}, {{Weapon|Fragor Prime}}, {{WF|Ash Prime}}, {{Weapon|Vectis Prime}}, and [[Carrier Prime]] from November 19th, 2019 to February 11th, 2020.

==Notes==
*The short reload time and the fast fire rate make {{M|Pressurized Magazine}} in conjunction with {{M|Pistol Ammo Mutation}} a viable modding choice.
*Can combine its exclusive mod {{M|Zazvat-Kar}} and a rank 1 or higher {{Arcane|Akimbo Slip Shot}} to achieve 100% ammo efficiency while aim gliding. Note that combining the Zazvat-Kar with {{A|Energized Munitions}} instead will only yield 93.75% ammo efficiency, as Energized Munitions stacks multiplicatively with other sources of ammo efficiency.

==Trivia==
*While Primed weapons usually have increases across almost all stats, the Akstiletto Prime features noticeably slower fire rate compared to the normal Akstiletto, though this translates into increased accuracy as is mentioned in the description.
*The Akstiletto Prime, alongside {{Weapon|Afuris Prime}}, {{Weapon|Akbolto Prime}}, {{Weapon|Aksomati Prime}}, {{Weapon|Ballistica Prime}}, {{Weapon|Cernos Prime}}, {{Weapon|Dual Kamas Prime}}, {{Weapon|Dual Keres Prime}}, {{Weapon|Fang Prime}}, {{Weapon|Gunsen Prime}}, {{Weapon|Paris Prime}} and {{Weapon|Zhuge Prime}} are the only Prime weapons that do not require [[Orokin Cell]]s as crafting ingredients.
*Though missing from their display image, the Akstiletto Prime have their magazines mounted on top, with lights on their rear and sides that indicate the level of ammunition remaining in each magazine, going off from top-down as the Stilettos are fired.
**Unlike the regular {{Weapon|Akstiletto}}, which both magazines' lights turn off at the same time, the Akstiletto Prime's lights go off consecutively, one Stiletto then the other one.
**Using black energy in the ''Smoke'' Palette or very dark energy colors will make it impossible or difficult to note the lights on the magazines.

